# Code owners for cadre.
#
# Deliberately one person rather than an org-wide team: a team of everyone
# means any member can approve anything, which turns the review gate into a
# formality. One named owner is a real gate.
#
# ⚠️ Consequence worth knowing: GitHub does not let a PR author approve their
# own PR. With a single code owner, a PR *you* open cannot satisfy
# "Require review from Code Owners" — you will need either a second owner, or
# admin bypass left enabled on the branch rule. See .github/DEPLOYMENT.md.

